senses.gloss:
प्र-√ 1. दा P. -ददाति, rarely Ā. -दत्ते, (Ved. inf. प्र॑-दातोस्, TS.; irreg. Pot. P. -ददेत्, Hcat.),
to give away, give, offer, present, grant, bestow, RV. &c. &c. (with or scil. भार्याम्, to give in marriage; with प्रतिवचस्, to g˚ an answer; with प्रवृत्तिम्, to information about an event; with युद्धम्, to g˚ battle; with द्वंद्व-युद्धम्, to engage in single combat; with विद्याम्, to communicate or impart knowledge; with हुताशनम्, to set fire to);
to give up, abolish, TS.;
to sell (with instr. of price), Pañcat.;
to restore (anything lost &c.), Mn.;
to pay, discharge (a debt), Yājñ.;
to put or place in (loc.), ib.; MBh. :
Pass. -दीयते, to be given away, be given, Mn.; MBh. &c.:
Caus. -दापयति, to cause to give, TS. &c. &c.;
to compel to give back or to repay, Yājñ.; Kull. ;
to cause to put in or to, MBh.; Bhpr.;
to put or place in (loc.), Car.;
 (with वस्तिम्), to apply a clyster, ib. :
Desid. -दित्सते, to wish to give in marriage, Daś.

प्र-√ दिश् P. Ā. -दिशति, ˚ते, to point out, show, indicate, declare, appoint, fix, ordain, RV. &c. &c.;
to direct, bid, urge, R.;
to assign, apportion, grant, Mn.; MBh. (-दिश्यति, i, 6472), Kāv. &c.:
Caus. -देशयति, to urge on, incite, MBh.; R. :
Intens. (pr. p. -दे॑दिशत्), to animate, RV.

प्र-√ दुष् P. -दुष्यति, to become worse, deteriorate, Suśr.;
to be defiled or polluted, fall (morally), Mn.; Yājñ.;
to commit an offence against (acc.), MBh.;
to become faithless, fall off, ib. :
Caus. -दूषयति, to spoil, deprave, corrupt, pollute, defile, MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to abuse, blame, censure, R.;
 (with चित्तम्) to be angry, Divyāv.

प्र-√ द्रु P. -द्रवति (ep. also Ā. ˚ते), to run forwards, run away, flee, RV. &c. &c.;
to hasten towards, rush upon or against (acc.), MBh.; R.;
to escape safely to (acc.), MBh. (v.l. प्राद्˚) :
Caus. -द्रावयति, to cause to run away, put to flight, MBh.
